tttools 2.0 (10-Nov-2026)

deflateTT, inflateTT and inflateTT-MP are version 2.0. The previous
public versions were deflateTT 1.21, inflateTT 1.2 and inflateTT-MP 1.3.

Compressor

An empty Huffman alphabet and a one-symbol alphabet now get two real
length-1 codes, the same way zlib fills a short alphabet. A file with
no 3-byte match used to crash, and a run of identical bytes produced a
DEFc file the decompressor could not read.

Code lengths are limited to 15 bits. Lengths that grow past 15 are
folded back with the same overflow adjustment zlib uses in gen_bitlen,
counting internal nodes as well as leaves. The decoder still accepts
codes up to 31 bits, so an older file that actually decompressed still
works. New files do not emit a longer code.

Matches are greedy LZ77 over a 32768-byte window, found with a 3-byte
hash chain. The longest match wins, and an equal length keeps the nearer
one. The maximum match is 258 bytes. There is no lazy matching.

deflate_bytes() is the library entry. File reads, writes and allocations
are checked, and a file that does not fit in an int is rejected. Lengths,
capacities and indexes in our own code are int. size_t is not used.

Decompressor

One decoder lives in inflateTT-MP. The inflateTT program is file I/O
around that library. inflate() takes the source length, the output
capacity and a caller-owned InflateContext, and returns a distinct
error for a bad argument, a truncated buffer, a bad header, a bad
Huffman code, a bad distance, a short output buffer, and a size that
does not match the header. It does not walk off either buffer.

inflate_vram16() is the same decoder with little-endian 16-bit stores,
so the destination can be Nintendo DS VRAM. The pointer must be 2-byte
aligned. inflate_ds.c compiles that entry as inflate() and keeps one
static context. Link it instead of inflate.o. The old inflateTT-DS
directory is gone. A program that supplies its own context calls
inflate_vram16() and compiles inflate.c.

The container format is documented in the repository README. It is
MSB-first, one block, with a custom code-length header. It is not zlib,
gzip, or a raw deflate stream. Literal, length and distance symbols
follow RFC 1951.

Tests

tests/roundtrip.c checks the Huffman limits, round trips, the 32768-byte
window edge, a 258-byte match, and malformed streams. The program is
built as tests.exe in the repository root. Cygwin's run looks for that
executable before the tests directory, so "run tests" starts it.
"make test" runs it and prints the results. "run -wait tests" returns
the suite's status. run hides the program's console.
